---
import ArrowIcon from "../components/ArrowIcon.astro";
import CopyTextButton from "../components/CopyTextButton.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const installCommand = `composer create-project ph7software/ph7builder:${site.latestRelease} my-dating-app --no-dev --prefer-dist`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Get pH7Builder" description="Install the latest published pH7Builder release through Composer or download the source from GitHub." path="/get-started/">
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Get pH7Builder</p>
    <h1>Start from the published open-source foundation.</h1>
    <p class="lede">pH7Builder {site.latestRelease} is the latest published release. Use Composer for a repeatable source installation or inspect the repository before deciding how your product should extend it.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="section surface">
    <div class="shell get-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status-pill">Recommended</span>
        <h2>Install through Composer</h2>
        <pre><code>{installCommand}</code></pre>
        <CopyTextButton value={installCommand} label="Copy install command" successMessage="Install command copied." />
        <p>This installs the current published release and creates an independent application copy with locked production dependencies. Future application upgrades are explicit rather than automatic Composer library updates.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/ai-builders/">Follow the AI builder path<ArrowIcon /></a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status-pill">Source</span>
        <h2>Review it on GitHub</h2>
        <p>Read the production quick start, project conventions, current release notes and open-source licence before deployment.</p>
        <p><a href={`${site.docsUrl}/QUICK_START.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the production quick start<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> before setting up a public site.</p>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href={site.githubUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the repository<ArrowIcon /><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section narrow-shell prose">
    <h2>Evaluate locally before deploying</h2>
    <p>Want to explore the software on your own machine? Follow the <a href={`${site.githubUrl}#local-evaluation-with-docker`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">local Docker instructions</a> to run a disposable test installation. No account, demo booking or meeting is required. Keep test data separate from anything you need to preserve.</p>
    <h2>Production requirements</h2>
    <p>pH7Builder {site.latestRelease} supports PHP 8.3 through 8.5 and requires MySQL 8.0 or newer, HTTPS, URL rewriting, and Apache or nginx. Composer 2 is required only for a source installation; the versioned release ZIP includes locked production dependencies. Read the <a href={`${site.docsUrl}/QUICK_START.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">release quick start<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a> for the complete extension and server requirements.</p>
    <p>The release page includes a SHA-256 checksum, SPDX SBOM and build metadata. Existing installations must follow the documented manual upgrade path and rehearse restoration before changing production; automatic in-place upgrades are not available.</p>
    <h2>Before real members arrive</h2>
    <p>Configure HTTPS, email delivery, backups, scheduled work and web-server rules for production. Review privacy and moderation decisions for the launch market. Then run the critical member journeys in the deployed environment.</p>
    <p><a href="/tools/dating-site-launch-checklist/">Use the dating product launch checklist</a> to keep those product and operational decisions together.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .get-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
  .get-grid article { display: flex; min-width: 0; min-height: 28rem; flex-direction: column; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--paper-strong); }
  .get-grid h2 { margin: auto 0 1rem; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem); }
  .get-grid pre { overflow-x: auto; padding: 1rem; background: var(--ink); color: white; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .8rem; }
  .get-grid .button { width: fit-content; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .get-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
